    <p>The Site uses cookies and similar technologies to collect usage data and to enhance your browsing experience. Cookies are small data files stored on your device that help us recognise returning visitors, remember preferences, and understand how the Site is used. Cookies used for analytics are set only after you accept them in the banner shown on your first visit, and everything on the Site works if you decline. HubSpot, which we use to handle enquiries, sets its cookies only after you accept.</p>
    {#- Added 26 Aug 2026 with Cloudflare Web Analytics. It is named here rather
        than left under "similar technologies" because it is the one thing on the
        site that measures visitors without asking first, and the reason it is
        allowed to is precisely that it stores nothing. If it is ever swapped for
        something that sets a cookie, that tool belongs behind the consent
        banner and this paragraph stops being true. -#}
    <p>We also use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views and understand which pages are read. It does not set cookies, does not store anything on your device, and does not follow you to other websites, which is why it runs without asking for consent. It records the page visited, the referring site, and general information such as country and device type. It does not identify you.</p>
    {#- Added 3 Sep 2026 with PostHog. Named for the same reason Cloudflare is.
        Each sentence is enforced in code, which is why the wording is
        registered in docs/claim-review.yml and rewording it fails the build:
        "sets no cookie" until Accept is cookieless_mode on_reject in the
        loader in base.njk; "a note that you have not accepted" is the opt-out
        flag PostHog keeps in localStorage, the same kind of record as the
        banner's own; "changes every day" is the daily salt on the server-side
        hash; "may record how a page was used" is session replay, which
        PostHog refuses to run for anyone who has not accepted, and can be
        dropped if replay is ever switched off in the project; "anything you
        type into a form hidden" is replay's default input masking; the EU is
        the region the project was created in. If any of those change in the
        code, this paragraph changes in the same commit. -#}
    <p>We also use PostHog to understand which pages are read and what visitors click on, so we can improve the Site. Until you accept cookies it sets no cookie, and the only thing kept on your device is a note that you have not accepted; visitors are counted using an anonymised identifier that changes every day and cannot be traced back to you. If you accept cookies, PostHog sets a cookie so that return visits can be recognised and may record how a page was used, with anything you type into a form hidden. PostHog stores this data in the European Union.</p>
    <p>You may manage or disable cookies through your browser settings. Please note that disabling cookies may affect certain features or functionality of the Site. For detailed information on cookie management, consult your browser's documentation.</p>
    {#- Added 24 Aug 2026 with the LinkedIn strip on the Insights page. The
        commitment in the second sentence is enforced in code, not by habit:
        the posts ship as cards with a button and the frame is only created
        once that button is pressed (see the click-to-load block in main.js).
        If anyone ever replaces that with a plain iframe, this paragraph
        becomes untrue, which is the reason both files say so. -#}
    <p>Some pages on the Site display posts published on our LinkedIn page. These are loaded directly from LinkedIn, which may set its own cookies on your device and is governed by LinkedIn's privacy policy rather than this one. Such a post is only loaded if you choose to open it: until you do, nothing is requested from LinkedIn and no LinkedIn cookies are set.</p>

    <h3>Data Sharing and Third Parties</h3>
    <p>Natural Trace does not sell, rent, or trade your personal data. We may share data with trusted third-party service providers who assist in operating the Site and delivering our services, subject to confidentiality obligations. We may also disclose information where required by law or to protect the rights, property, or safety of Natural Trace, our users, or the public.</p>
    <p>This Privacy Policy does not govern the practices of third-party websites or services linked from the Site. We encourage you to review the privacy policies of any third-party services you access.</p>

    <h3>Data Retention</h3>
    <p>We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes outlined in this policy, or as required by applicable law. When personal data is no longer needed, we will securely delete or anonymise it.</p>

    <h3>Data Security</h3>
    <p>We implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction. However, no method of transmission over the Internet or electronic storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>

    <h3>Your Rights Under the GDPR</h3>
    <p>If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA) or the United Kingdom, you are entitled to the following rights under the General Data Protection Regulation:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong>: Request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Rectification</strong>: Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete personal data.</li>
      <li><strong>Erasure</strong>: Request deletion of your personal data, subject to applicable legal exceptions.</li>
      <li><strong>Restriction of Processing</strong>: Request that we limit the processing of your personal data under certain circumstances.</li>
      <li><strong>Objection</strong>: Object to the processing of your personal data where we rely on legitimate interests as the legal basis.</li>
      <li><strong>Data Portability</strong>: Request transfer of your personal data to another organisation in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us at the address below. We will respond to verified requests within one month, as required by law.</p>

    <h3>Your Rights Under the CCPA</h3>
    <p>If you are a California resident, the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) provides you with the following rights:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The right to know what personal data we collect, use, and disclose about you.</li>
      <li>The right to request deletion of personal data we have collected from you.</li>
      <li>The right to opt out of the sale of your personal data. Natural Trace does not sell personal data.</li>
      <li>The right to non-discrimination for exercising your privacy rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To submit a request, please contact us at the address below. We will respond within the timeframes required by applicable law.</p>

    <h3>Singapore PDPA</h3>
    <p>As a Singapore-registered company, Natural Trace complies with the Personal Data Protection Act 2012 (PDPA). You may request access to or correction of your personal data held by us. To withdraw consent for the collection, use, or disclosure of your personal data, please contact our Data Protection Officer at the address below.</p>

    <h3>Children's Privacy</h3>
    <p>The Site is not directed at individuals under the age of 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal data from children. If we become aware that we have inadvertently collected personal data from a child under 13, we will take prompt steps to delete such data. If you believe a child has provided us with personal data, please contact us immediately.</p>

    <h3>Changes to This Policy</h3>
    <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or applicable law. Any material changes will be posted on this page with a revised effective date. We encourage you to review this policy periodically.</p>

    <h3>Contact Us</h3>
    <p>For questions, requests, or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy or our data practices, please contact:</p>
